{"findings":[{"file":"cookiecutter/config.py","line":48,"what_goes_wrong":"A configuration whose default_context contains a dictionary for a new variable raises KeyError instead of loading the valid nested default.","trigger":"Load a YAML config containing default_context: {service: {port: 8080}}.","expected":"The loaded default_context should contain service mapped to {'port': 8080}.","actual":"merge_configs accesses default['service'] even though that template-defined key is absent from the empty built-in default_context, raising KeyError.","confidence":"high","verified_by_running":true,"reproduction":"import tempfile\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom cookiecutter.config import get_config\n\nwith tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as directory:\n    config = Path(directory) / 'config.yaml'\n    config.write_text('default_context:\\n  service:\\n    port: 8080\\n', encoding='utf-8')\n    assert get_config(str(config))['default_context']['service'] == {'port': 8080}\n"},{"file":"cookiecutter/vcs.py","line":32,"what_goes_wrong":"Explicit git/hg URLs containing a plus sign in their path are parsed as an unknown-format URL and retain the git+ prefix.","trigger":"Call identify_repo('git+https://example.test/team/c++-template.git').","expected":"It should return ('git', 'https://example.test/team/c++-template.git'), preserving the plus in the repository path while removing only the type prefix.","actual":"split('+') produces more than two parts, so the function returns a URL still beginning git+, which clone cannot use as an HTTPS URL.","confidence":"high","verified_by_running":true,"reproduction":"from cookiecutter.vcs import identify_repo\n\nassert identify_repo('git+https://example.test/team/c++-template.git') == (\n    'git', 'https://example.test/team/c++-template.git'\n)\n"},{"file":"cookiecutter/vcs.py","line":82,"what_goes_wrong":"Repository names containing '.git' anywhere other than a final suffix are truncated, so clone returns and uses the wrong target directory.","trigger":"Clone git+https://example.test/org/template.git.backup into a directory, with no checkout required.","expected":"Git's default clone directory is template.git.backup, and Cookiecutter should return that path.","actual":"The computed path is template because rsplit('.git')[0] removes the middle portion; a requested checkout consequently runs in a nonexistent directory.","confidence":"high","verified_by_running":true,"reproduction":"import tempfile\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport cookiecutter.vcs as vcs\n\nwith tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as directory:\n    vcs.is_vcs_installed = lambda _: True\n    vcs.subprocess.check_output = lambda *args, **kwargs: b''\n    actual = vcs.clone(\n        'git+https://example.test/org/template.git.backup', clone_to_dir=directory\n    )\n    assert actual == str(Path(directory) / 'template.git.backup')\n"},{"file":"cookiecutter/find.py","line":20,"what_goes_wrong":"Template discovery can select a templated file instead of the project-template directory.","trigger":"A repository root contains both cookiecutter{{cookiecutter.name}}.txt and the real {{cookiecutter.name}} directory, with the file encountered first by listdir.","expected":"find_template should return the directory, as its documentation states.","actual":"It accepts the file solely because its name contains cookiecutter and Jinja delimiters, returning a non-directory path and causing later generation to fail.","confidence":"high","verified_by_running":true,"reproduction":"import os\nimport tempfile\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom cookiecutter.find import find_template\n\nwith tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as directory:\n    root = Path(directory)\n    (root / 'cookiecutter{{cookiecutter.name}}.txt').write_text('', encoding='utf-8')\n    (root / '{{cookiecutter.name}}').mkdir()\n    original_listdir = os.listdir\n    os.listdir = lambda path: ['cookiecutter{{cookiecutter.name}}.txt', '{{cookiecutter.name}}']\n    try:\n        assert find_template(str(root)) == str(root / '{{cookiecutter.name}}')\n    finally:\n        os.listdir = original_listdir\n"},{"file":"cookiecutter/cli.py","line":26,"what_goes_wrong":"The version banner reports Python 3.10 and later as Python 3.1.","trigger":"Run the CLI under Python 3.10.x or any later two-digit minor version.","expected":"The banner should include the complete major.minor version, e.g. Python 3.10.","actual":"sys.version[:3] truncates the version after the first minor digit.","confidence":"high","verified_by_running":true,"reproduction":"import cookiecutter.cli as cli\n\ncli.sys.version = '3.10.12 (main, Jan 1 2026) [MSC]'\nassert 'Python 3.10' in cli.version_msg()\n"}],"what_examined":"Reviewed all Python modules under cookiecutter, traced configuration, repository discovery, VCS, generation, hook, prompt, and archive flows, and ran Ruff as a lead source. I ran pytest until its environment temp-directory permission blocker (24 tests passed; then WinError 5 creating pytest-of-hollo) and executed each reported reproduction against the code."}
